      "card_ids": ["C02","C03","C07","C09","C10","C15"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Pyrimidine nucleoside analogs with similarly polar profiles show high absolute oral bioavailability: lamivudine 69–93% across doses and formulations (C04, C06, C14, C19, C22, C23), emtricitabine 92% (C18, C25), and zalcitabine 80% in humans (C16) with 30% in fasted mice (C24).",
      "card_ids": ["C04","C06","C14","C19","C22","C23","C18","C25","C16","C24"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records show rapid absorption and measurable plasma exposure for related nucleoside analogs: lamivudine median Tmax 0.75–1.0 h and Cmax 3.3 µg/mL (C26, C28, C30), steady-state AUC0-12 5522.7 ng·h/mL (C36), and penciclovir Cmax ~3.4 µg/mL after oral famciclovir (C31, C34).",
      "card_ids": ["C26","C28","C30","C36","C31","C34"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 intestinal absorption/solubility records for related nucleosides are supportive: ribavirin and ganciclovir are highly soluble (C38, C39, C41, C48), lamivudine shows net absorptive jejunal flux (A→B 1.110 vs B→A 0.093 ×10^-8 mol/min; C40, C44), and acyclovir tablets dissolve almost completely within 20 min (C47).",
      "card_ids": ["C38","C39","C40","C41","C44","C47","C48"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No supplied record provides affirmative evidence of F < 20% for a relevant nucleoside analog; the lowest relevant values are didanosine 22–28% and mouse zalcitabine 30%, both above the threshold (C03, C09, C24).",
      "card_ids": ["C03","C09","C24"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C38","C39","C40","C41","C42","C43","C44","C45","C46","C47","C48","C49"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule is present in the supplied records.",
    "No direct permeability, efflux, or first-pass data for the query; L4 permeability evidence is for lamivudine, and solubility/dissolution records are for other nucleosides.",
    "The query prandial state is unspecified; most evidence is fasted, but the fed cladribine record (40.5%) still exceeds the threshold.",
    "Structural differences between the cyclobutane carbocyclic guanine nucleoside and the deoxyribose/oxathiolane/acyclic nucleoside analogs could affect permeability or first-pass extraction; the closest low-margin analog (didanosine 22–28%) leaves a narrow margin above the 20% threshold.",
    "Some L3 exposure records involve prodrugs (famciclovir to penciclovir, adefovir dipivoxil to adefovir), so their oral exposure does not directly inform the non-prodrug query."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high because all transferable nucleoside analog contexts, including the lowest relevant values (didanosine 22–28% and mouse zalcitabine 30%), exceed the 20% threshold; L3 oral exposure records and L4 solubility/permeability records add supportive but indirect evidence of rapid absorption, high solubility, and net absorptive flux for related nucleosides, and no supplied record provides affirmative evidence for F < 20%; confidence remains moderate due to lack of a direct query measurement and structural differences."
}

